    <string-array name="health_tips">
        <item>Always store medications in a cool, dry place away from direct sunlight.</item>
        <item>Always check the expiration date on medicine packages before consumption.</item>
        <item>Never share your prescribed medicines with family or friends.</item>
        <item>Always read the medicine package label carefully for important instructions.</item>
        <item>Do not consume alcohol while taking medications to avoid severe reactions.</item>
        <item>Store all medicines safely out of reach and sight of young children.</item>
        <item>Complete your full course of antibiotics even if you start feeling better.</item>
        <item>Consult your physician before stopping any long-term prescription medication.</item>
        <item>Inform your doctor or pharmacist about any known drug allergies you have.</item>
        <item>Drink plenty of water when swallowing oral tablets and capsules.</item>
        <item>Keep medicines in their original packaging to avoid confusion.</item>
        <item>Do not crush or break enteric-coated or sustained-release tablets.</item>
        <item>Store liquid syrups in an upright position and use the provided measuring cap.</item>
        <item>Dispose of expired or leftover medications safely according to guidelines.</item>
        <item>Take your medications at the same scheduled time every day for best results.</item>
        <item>Never double your dose if you accidentally miss a scheduled medicine.</item>
        <item>Check if your medicine should be taken before or after meals.</item>
        <item>Keep an updated physical list of all your current active medications.</item>
        <item>Avoid storing medicines in bathroom cabinets due to heat and humidity.</item>
        <item>Always double-check medicine names if you receive a new refill.</item>
    </string-array>
